ECHNIQUES.md from "USED PARTIAL — orbit-dim sub-frame" to "USED PARTIAL — orbit-dim and first-order tangent sub-frames". **Falsifier**: any homogeneous d, n ∈ {4, 5} where matched-support baseline `dim T_{g_d}` differs from f_chi_P, OR where the torus weight set differs. None found across 15 trials × 8 (n, d) cells = 120 total cells. **Successor (S212, slot 2/5)**: compute `I_2(tilde f_chi_P^{(4)})` for the homogenised polynomial of degree 3 in 5 variables, identify which `S_λ` (with `|λ| = 6`) occur in `Sym^2(Sym^3 V_5) / I_2`, compare with `det_2 · y^2`-orbit and matched-support random baselines — the actual second-order Mulmuley-Sohoni occurrence-obstruction test. See `experiments/algebraic/gct_chi_p_orbit/plethysm_subframe.py`, `experiments/algebraic/gct_chi_p_orbit/plethysm_subframe_results.md`, `archive/sessions/session211_commit_a7_plethysm_subframe.md`. | 211 |
    
    
